       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for ibuprofen in adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks at this dose:** The risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove them.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 400\u2013600 mg by mouth every 6 hours (typical for pain or inflammation)\n- 1600 mg total per day, divided\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you want, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note on the order. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
